Local-First Sovereign Execution

Status: Accepted

Context: 
- AI workflows today are mostly focused on using the best models over the cloud or through dedicated APIs. 
  This means your data must leave on-prem, secure environments to one or more third parties. 
  This is an impossible ask for data in sectors like healthcare, defense, or finance.

Decision: 
- Project must focus on workflow and agent lifecycle management from cradle to grave on local hardware.

Consequences: 
- Local AI requires orchestration mechanisms for memory management, scheduling, and stability across CPU, Memory, and GPU. 
- Scalability will be a significant challenge as workflow count increases.
- Local models have more limited intelligence.
- Hardware may be non-heterogeneous (multiple different GPUs/nodes), and must be accounted for.

